%erg 0.1
Title: erg log refuses archived tickets with a misleading 'no ticket found'
Created: 2026-11-11
Author: MinhHaDuong

--- log ---
2026-11-11T10:56Z MinhHaDuong created

--- body ---
## Context

Incident reported from climate-finance-het (raid of 2026-11-11). After a PR
closed ticket 0303 there, the raid had to append a review bump to it (`note
verify-reroll — round 1: …`). `erg close 0303` had already moved the file to
`tickets/closed/` (the follow-up `erg archive 0303` answered "no ticket
found"), and then:

    $ tickets/erg log 0303 "note verify-reroll — …" tickets
    log: no ticket found for ID 0303 in tickets

The note could not be recorded on the ticket. The harness forbids hand-written
log lines, so the fact went to a journal and the review notes instead of the
ticket's own log.

Observed in the source, cause not yet confirmed by a test:
`src/go/log.go:98` resolves through `resolveTicketByID`
(`src/go/main.go:180`), which globs `<dir>/<id>-*.erg` only and never looks in
`<dir>/closed/`. So the refusal looks like a side effect of lookup scope, not
a deliberate policy, and the message says "not found" for a ticket that
exists.

## Why it matters

Closed tickets legitimately receive log lines: review bumps, post-merge notes,
reopening rationale, cross-project hand-offs. The barrier pushes agents
toward hand edits of an append-only log, or toward dropping the fact.

## Stance (author, 2026-11-11)

The block is an unnecessary barrier. Minimum now: make the behaviour explicit,
either resolve the ID in `closed/` as well, or refuse with a message that
names the archived file and how to proceed. **If the block recurs, consider
changing the stance to "accept and warn"**: append to the archived ticket and
print a one-line warning that the ticket is closed, rather than refusing.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `erg log <id>` on an archived ticket either appends (accept-and-warn) or
      refuses with a message naming `closed/<file>`, never "no ticket found"
- [ ] The choice and its reason are recorded in this ticket's log
- [ ] A test covers `erg log` on a ticket under `closed/`
- [ ] Other commands sharing `resolveTicketByID` (e.g. `show`) are checked
      for the same blind spot and listed
